[2026-05-24T12:47:04.043Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_314","type":"reasoning","text":"**Finalizing PR Review**\n\nI’m trying to finalize the process. First, I need to check the output status from the command `git status --short`, which will show no changes just the branch name. I should also consider verifying the PR body for the \"Fixes\" syntax. It seems like I need to ensure the PR title and description are updated and examine the body for any necessary edits. Also, I should confirm that there are no uncommitted changes and that the default branch is merged.\n**Verifying Merge Status**\n\nI need to check if the default branch is merged into the PR branch. First, I might determine the merge base by checking if the branch is behind the main one. This could involve fetching updates from the origin for safety. I’ll run `git fetch origin main` followed by `git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/main`. If the branch is behind, I must decide whether to merge it. I’ll use `gh pr view --json baseRefName` to check this, and then see if I need to merge the latest changes.\n**Checking Merge and CI**\n\nI’m thinking that this process could create a commit and trigger CI, which seems a bit excessive, but it might be necessary based on the instructions. I need to finalize by checking if the default branch is merged into the PR branch. If it's not merged, I might need to merge it, but only if it’s behind. I’ll verify this and also look into the body. I could use parallel queries for fetching and viewing the base. Let’s fetch and determine the status."}}
