issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/234","id":4528554549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABDexCNQ","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-24T12:06:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T12:10:43Z","body":"I don't see in tests exact examples of answers, only contains and not contains. I need more detailed examples so tests are like docs, give exact variations. So the answer should one of multiple possibilities, and it should as explicit as possible, so it will be easy to understand how system works only by looking each concrete test. So everything should be in addition to contains and not contains, just more explicit, and easier to read for the system architect.\r\n\r\nAlso make sure we also context/environment aware, not all features are available locally in CLI, on a server as a service, in web browser environment and so on. So when executed in different environments the system should be self aware and context aware so it will not talk about features, that are not available in specific environment.\r\n\r\nAlso I want the same style to be demanded for all other tests, we need a test or CI/CD rule that will guarantee it, so you will be forced to make every test about the system in such explicit way.\r\n\r\nAlso we should use proper `Fixes https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/146` syntax in pull request description to fully close all the issues. Word `Addresses` is not recognized by GitHub as explicit link to the issue, that will cause it to automatically close on pull request merge.\r\n\r\nWe need to ensure all changes are correct, consistent, validated, tested, documented, logged and fully meet each and all discussed requirements in deepest and widest possible sense (check issue description and all comments in issue and in pull request, make sure each and every requirement listed before actually checking if they were addressed). The scope is the entire repository, every change in one place should also be applied in all places in the codebase and docs. Ensure all CI/CD checks pass.\r\n\r\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4528554549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/comments/4528570364","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/234#issuecomment-4528570364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/234","id":4528570364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABDex__A","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","